.TH HCC2D_STREAMER 1 "August 2026" "HCC2D CLI C Streamer 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hcc2d_streamer \- transfer files through streams of QR or HCC2D symbols
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hcc2d_streamer
[\fIoptions\fR]
\fIFILE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBhcc2d_streamer\fR reads a file, optionally compresses it, splits it into
dynamic Reed-Solomon erasure groups, and displays the resulting shards as a
repeating sequence of QR, HCC2D4, or HCC2D8 symbols in an SDL2 window.
The HCC2D Decoder companion app captures the sequence and reconstructs the
original file.
.PP
Symbols are generated in memory and are not written to temporary image files.
.PP
This public CLI supports only QR, HCC2D4, and HCC2D8 with symbol versions 1 to
40. Experimental HCC2D16 and experimental version 45 are not included.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fBqr\fR|\fBhcc2d4\fR|\fBhcc2d8\fR
Select the symbol family. The default is \fBhcc2d8\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-colors\fR \fB2\fR|\fB4\fR|\fB8\fR
Select the same symbol family by palette size: 2 means QR, 4 means HCC2D4,
and 8 means HCC2D8. This option is mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-mode\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-ec-level\fR \fBL\fR|\fBM\fR|\fBQ\fR|\fBH\fR
Set the error-correction level inside each symbol. The default is \fBM\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fIN\fR
Set the fixed symbol version from 1 to 40. The default is 30.
.TP
\fB\-\-fps\fR \fIN\fR
Set the display rate from 10 to 20 symbols per second. The default is 10.
.TP
\fB\-\-display\fR \fIN\fR
Select the SDL display index used for window placement and size calculation.
The default is 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet-zone\fR \fIN\fR
Set the quiet zone from 0 to 16 modules. The default is 4.
.TP
\fB\-\-no-titlebar\fR
Hide window decorations so that more display height is available to the
symbol.
.TP
\fB\-\-palette-rgb\fR \fILIST\fR
Set a complete custom HCC2D4 or HCC2D8 palette as a quoted list in the form
\fIR,G,B;R,G,B;...\fR. Index 0 must be black and the last index white.
This option is not valid with QR mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-k-max\fR \fIN\fR
Set the maximum number of data shards in one erasure group, from 1 to 254.
The default is 150.
.TP
\fB\-\-parity-num\fR \fIN\fR
Set the parity-ratio numerator. The default is 70.
.TP
\fB\-\-parity-den\fR \fIN\fR
Set the positive parity-ratio denominator. The default is 100.
The program rejects combinations for which data plus parity would exceed 255
shards in one group.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show the built-in help text and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Stream a file with the default HCC2D8 profile:
.B hcc2d_streamer document.pdf
.TP
Stream HCC2D8 version 40 at 15 symbols per second:
.B hcc2d_streamer \-\-mode hcc2d8 \-\-ec-level L \-\-version 40 \-\-fps 15 document.pdf
.TP
Stream HCC2D4:
.B hcc2d_streamer \-\-mode hcc2d4 \-\-version 30 document.pdf
.TP
Stream standard QR Codes:
.B hcc2d_streamer \-\-mode qr \-\-version 20 document.pdf
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B hcc2d_streamer
returns 0 after the window is closed normally and a non-zero status on errors.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hcc2d_streamer
Installed command-line Streamer.
.SH SECURITY
The Streamer performs a local optical transfer and does not upload the input
file. Anyone able to observe and decode enough displayed symbols may recover
the file.
